BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pete Sawyer and the Left Hand Monkey Wrench Gang
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T183000
UID:69bb2ec51bf4ed5cc8a1c5fb@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:Pete Sawyer & The Left Hand Monkey Wrench Gang return to the O
 CA Amphitheater on Saturday August 29th for two fat sets of all killer- no
  filler Grateful Dead classics\, deep cuts and unexpected gems! Pete and T
 he Gang have been taking the West Coast by storm in 2026 and you will be m
 oved body and soul by their interplanetary exploration of the majestic Gra
 teful Dead songbook.\nPete is bringing an absolutely amazing band!\nThe Ga
 ng:\nElliott Peck (Phil Lesh\, Midnight North)\nMookie Siegel (Bob Weir\, 
 Phil Lesh)\nSean Nelson (Phil Lesh\, Chuck Prophet)\nJustin Purtill (JGB\,
  Residente)\nMatt Lazarus (Stu Allen\, Joint Chiefs\nTickets are $25/$20 f
 or OCA members. Online sales end 1 hour before showtime. Doors open at 3:3
 0 PM. No outside food/beverage (water OK). Bring your own cushion\, blanke
 t or low-backed chair.\nGet tickets\n“Pete Sawyer & The Left Hand Monkey
  Wrench Gang is one of the most compelling recent entries into the world o
 f Grateful Dead Tributes” — Nick Sestanovich\, The Santa Cruz Sentinal
 \n"From the first note to the final encore\, audiences can expect a night 
 of inspired musicianship\, soulful improvisation\, and a musical chemistry
  that only forms when top-tier artists share the stage. Drawing from the d
 eep well of classic rock\, psychedelia\, and the storied traditions of the
  Grateful Dead and other influential pioneers\, Pete Sawyer and The Left H
 and Monkey Wrench Gang transport listeners on a sonic journey that pays tr
 ibute to the past while forging ahead into new musical territory.” —\n
 GratefulWeb.com\n“My first visit to the Tabard Theatre was this past wee
 kend to see Pete Sawyer & the Left-Hand Monkey Wrench Gang. The band's pro
 mise of "all killer\, no filler" Grateful Dead music was an understatement
 . They are as good as any band of that genre that I have ever seen (DSO\, 
 Grateful Shred\, JRAD\, etc.).” Michael Palmini (\nrelix.com\n)
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts\, 3850 Doris Murphy Court\, Occide
 ntal\, CA 95465
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/pete-sawyer
 -and-the-left-hand-monkey-wrench-gang
X-SOURCE:Occidental Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sound Bath with Laura Benson
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260908T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260908T203000
UID:69ade3567be1e075a8dd6f59@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:Rest & Renew at our Sound Bath!\nSupport your nervous system\,
  release anxiety and stress\, and harmonize your body\, mind and spirit on
  the 2nd Tuesday of every month! Laura Benson has a Masters in Intuition M
 edicine(R) and is a certified sound healer who will guide you through a ge
 ntle meditation before each sound bath session. Bring your own yoga mat & 
 blanket and come ready to rest and renew! In the OCA Studio.\nSliding scal
 e pricing $25-$35.\nRegister\nA sound bath is a whole-body\, immersive lis
 tening experience. During a sound bath\, participants often sit or lie dow
 n\, and are surrounded by the mostly non-melodic soundscapes created by a 
 range of instruments played by the sound bath facilitator. Hence\, they ar
 e “bathed” in sound.\nSound therapy is a non-invasive healing modality
  that utilizes the physical and physiological interactions of sound on our
  bodies and nervous systems to produce therapeutic results. In a sound hea
 ling session\, specific sonic frequencies are used to soothe the central n
 ervous system\, calm the breath\, and quiet the mind by encouraging the br
 ain to move into more relaxed states\, down from beta (fight-or-flight) an
 d into theta and alpha waves. This increases present-moment awareness and 
 reduces stress and anxiety. Sound baths have been found to be effective in
  improving mood\, cognitive function\, and overall mental\, physical\, and
  spiritual wellbeing.\nCrystal bowl sound baths are particularly powerful 
 in that each bowl is tuned to a specific frequency that corresponds with a
  different chakra\, or energy center\, of the body. Based on specific need
 s\, a practitioner can focus on releasing tension or clearing out stuck en
 ergy in specific chakras by playing certain bowls or intervals.\nWhile att
 ending a sound bath\, you may experience physical sensations brought out b
 y the crystal sound bowls or gong\, such as tingling in your limbs or scal
 p\, slowing of your breathing\, eye flutters\, or small muscle spasms. Not
  to worry! These sensations often indicate the release of tension or emoti
 onal energy stored in the body’s energy systems.
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts\, 3850 Doris Murphy Court\, Occide
 ntal\, CA 95465
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/rest-renew-
 monthly-sound-bath-l5n5c-wchlw-38gmc-rw262-hd6w3-nlnhm-bn8b8-d74pg-d79je-w
 x3an-ampe7-zckp7-gndtj-32c6f-4y8an-wsmxr-y3rtb-8k62p-lx4gx-36kl7-5kgyd
X-SOURCE:Occidental Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
